**`app/api/jobs/search/route.ts:210-226` — COUNT + SELECT: dos viajes a la BD**

```typescript
const countRes = await pool.query(`SELECT COUNT(*) FROM "JobListing" WHERE ${whereClause}`, params);
const dbResult = await pool.query(`SELECT id, title, ... FROM "JobListing" WHERE ${whereClause} ...`, params);
```

**Solución:** usar window function para obtener el total en la misma query:

```typescript
const sql = `
  SELECT id, title, company, city, province, salary, description,
         "sourceUrl", "sourceName", "scrapedAt",
         COUNT(*) OVER() AS total_count
  FROM "JobListing"
  WHERE ${whereClause}
  ORDER BY ...
  LIMIT $${idx} OFFSET $${idx + 1}
`;
const dbResult = await pool.query(sql, params);
const totalDB = dbResult.rows[0] ? parseInt(dbResult.rows[0].total_count) : 0;
```

Elimina un round-trip a PostgreSQL en cada búsqueda.

